PROPOSAL: product-direction decision for the maintainer; do not implement without a go-ahead.

Evidence: History.pm:31-33 requires `wiki_root/.git` to be a directory, so a wiki in a subdirectory of a repo or in a worktree fails (every write warns, history tools fail). With --git but no Git::Raw or no repo the server starts and only warns on each write.
Options: (a) `Git::Raw::Repository->discover` plus a repo-relative path prefix; (b) one clear startup warning when --git cannot be honoured (keeps the graceful degrade); (c) refuse to start in --git mode when the repo cannot be opened (contradicts the documented graceful degrade).
Recommendation: (b) now, (a) later.

2026-10-26 19:51 Decision (coordinator, on the maintainer's order to work the board off): options (a) + (b): Git::Raw::Repository->discover with a repo-relative prefix (subdirectories, worktrees); one startup warning when --git cannot be honoured, graceful degrade kept. Branch docker.
